Added:
- authenticated RPC method getmainnethealth
- qrx-cli getmainnethealth
- multi-node observatory with same-height block hash/state-root disagreement detection
- supply invariant and protocol upgrade alerting
- atomic qrxscan-friendly mainnet-health.json output + JSONL event log
- peer viewer for peer/known-peer/seed domains, IPs, ports, endpoint type/scope and optional DNS resolution
- explicit warning against publishing validator IP inventory publicly
- emergency activation-height readiness checker requiring lead blocks and >2/3 observed upgraded voting power
- operator documentation and example config

Known caveats:
- Existing compiler warnings remain and were not introduced by this phase.
- Observatory example intentionally queries local authenticated RPC/datadirs. Cross-host report transport must use a secure authenticated channel; do not expose rpc.token over plaintext HTTP.
- Peer viewer does not perform third-party GeoIP/ASN lookups; this avoids an external dependency and privacy leak. ASN/diversity can be added server-side using a vetted offline database.
- Operational monitoring does not replace independent consensus/cryptography audit or real multi-host testing.
